VALUES (651, '0', $t$ASK 651: the PROVEN IN check reads a quotation to the end of its line, not 160 characters$t$,
  $t$PRS refCheck tests whether a PROVEN IN round quotes the verse with its reference. It read only 160 characters after the reference, so when the closing quotation mark fell past character 160 the test failed and the verse was classed UNPROVEN with the reason "named there but not quoted with its reference". Luke 1:35 is 221 characters in the KJV: in run 42528 the defender's round DR1 quotes Luke 1:35 whole five times and all five hits failed, and the judges were told three times "Luke 1:35 (PROVEN IN [DR1]: the verse is named there but not quoted with its reference)". Change, one expression in each of four copies (D4 Build, Panel Build, Build Independent Verdict, Shared Library): the window runs from the reference to the end of that line. The quotation test itself is unchanged. Expected effect: a verse whose quotation is whole on its line reads PROVEN BY REFERENCE, in the Oracle's list of unproven presses and in the judges' press ledger. Not changed: ruling 398, the cap, the WALL-2024 floor, a model setting, reasoning. (plan rev 0, ask651/w4/plan651.md md5 a6d624d4)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$One build, one card and one write carry ASK 651 and ASK 652 together: target 1aa15175, written by W4 on the operator's press "Write it" at 09:09 CST 2026-11-25 on W4's card (Wall 12127; audit 42304), engine 7f4e5503 to 50ade174 (426 nodes; the child aad0ad9c unchanged), build graded PASS by W1 (Wall 12108: W1 ran b651 and b652 on its own live copy and the result equals the target in every node parameter and in the connections; only D4 Build, Panel Build, Build Independent Verdict and Shared Library change) and read back PASS by W1 (Wall 12129). IN PART, because no run has been made since the write. For ASK 651: plan rev 0 PASS WITH N1 (Wall 12101: the 160-character slice occurs once in each of the four nodes in live 7f4e5503 and the defect is confirmed; running the window to the end of the line changes nothing else, because the test already stops at a newline). N1 (in the Shared Library JSON-line copy the newline must be written escaped) is met in the build (Wall 12108). Offline replay (W4, Wall 12102, 12105): with 651 and 652 together the Oracle's list of unproven presses for 42528 holds only "premise 4: Luke 1:34", a WALL-2024 floor item held for the operator by the coordinator, and for 42373 "none". W4 corrected its own Wall 12100: the 8-character values there were sha256 prefixes; the plan of record by md5 is a6d624d4 (Wall 12102). NOT CHECKED by W1: W4's replay figures; W4's 18-of-18 match of the "before" replay to the live Panel Build output; the Library Check hashes; audit 42304. Open: two clean live runs. RUN REVISION 43103 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has been made, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-43103-gkg7el4e (debate_results 0731a1ea, row saved 11:20 CST 2026-11-27; the operator's launch 10:48 CST, ended 11:44 CST by W4's report, Wall 12767; engine 66ba992d and child aad0ad9c; google/gemini-4-hydrogen as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; outcome UNGRADED, panel 0-0 with 3 not counted under the debate rule; three judgments stored (sonnet, sol, sol62); cost 7.5384; no debate_errors row after the launch). FIRST RUN, NO REFUSAL SEEN; THE MARK ITSELF NOT READ. W4: Luke 1:35 (221 characters) was pressed and quoted whole, and no row of the enforcer prompts or judgments carries "named there but not quoted with its reference" (W1 by SQL: 0 rows). The panel's first prompt, where the press ledger stands, is not in the tables W4 read and was not read, so the line PROVEN BY REFERENCE for that verse is not shown. W3 does not count this run as one of the two live runs with no issue; objective_met and status are unchanged.$t$,
  '12100, 12101, 12102, 12105, 12108, 12127, 12129, 12139, 12145, 12152, 12787, 12791, 12797, 12799, 12800, 12802, 12803, 12804, 12789',
